WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.932 line:90%
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:05.710 line:90%
 Hi.

00:00:05.710 --> 00:00:08.050 line:10%
I'm Tamara Krinsky
for "Women of Marvel."

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:11.920 line:10%
And I am here with the legendary
singer, songwriter, and rock

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:14.900 line:10%
star, Nancy Wilson from Heart.

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:16.340 line:10%
Hey, Nancy, how's it going?

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:17.140 line:90%
 Really good.

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:18.530 line:90%
I'm better now.

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:20.180 line:84%
 Well, it's an honor to
be here with you today.

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:21.850 line:84%
And we're going to
talk about firsts.

00:00:21.850 --> 00:00:23.510 line:84%
So your song is in this
film, "Crazy on You."

00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:24.310 line:90%
 Yeah.

00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:27.010 line:84%
 And how did it
feel when the song

00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:28.660 line:90%
became a part of this film?

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:30.490 line:84%
 It's an honor
to be in the film

00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:32.049 line:84%
because the film
itself, I thought,

00:00:32.049 --> 00:00:36.380 line:84%
was so aspirational,
for women in particular.

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:37.590 line:84%
 You know what
is really amazing,

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:40.540 line:84%
I think, the way they
use music in this movie

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:42.080 line:90%
to help tell the story.

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:44.590 line:84%
And I mean, it's got the
first female composer

00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:45.970 line:84%
of a Marvel Studio's movie.
- I know.

00:00:45.970 --> 00:00:46.995 line:84%
 You know, you certainly--
NANCY WILSON: Director.

00:00:46.995 --> 00:00:48.430 line:84%
 --know something
about film composing.

00:00:48.430 --> 00:00:49.230 line:90%
So--

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:51.970 line:84%
 Yeah, it's just really great
to see teamwork like that

00:00:51.970 --> 00:00:57.010 line:84%
and women sort of being
encouraged now more

00:00:57.010 --> 00:01:01.480 line:84%
and allowed more, given the
opportunities like that.

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:04.629 line:84%
 So if you were going to give
a message to a lot of the girls

00:01:04.629 --> 00:01:07.000 line:84%
today about leadership and
what you need to do, what

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.230 line:90%
would you want to say to them?

00:01:08.230 --> 00:01:14.860 line:84%
 I think it's important
to lead with grace.

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:19.090 line:84%
Because if you push people
because you think you can lead

00:01:19.090 --> 00:01:22.030 line:84%
them, or get them to
do something, or make

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:25.120 line:84%
them do things, it's
never effective.

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:30.160 line:84%
But you have to be
strong gracefully.

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:30.970 line:90%
[LAUGHTER]

00:01:30.970 --> 00:01:31.890 line:84%
Yes.
- It's tough.

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:32.690 line:90%
Right?

00:01:32.690 --> 00:01:35.620 line:84%
 Well, people would always
tell me, like, what--

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:38.050 line:84%
how can you be
out front wielding

00:01:38.050 --> 00:01:42.520 line:84%
that great big guitar on
a big, loud rock stage

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:44.745 line:84%
and still maintain
your femininity?

00:01:44.745 --> 00:01:48.305 line:84%
And I was like, well,
being myself, I guess.

00:01:48.305 --> 00:01:49.480 line:84%
 Well, and I think
that's actually

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:51.940 line:84%
a theme of "Captain
Marvel," the things

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:53.120 line:90%
that you're passionate about.

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:55.330 line:84%
I mean, you're so passionate
about guitar playing.

00:01:55.330 --> 00:01:56.907 line:84%
And you've got a
character like Carol

00:01:56.907 --> 00:01:58.740 line:84%
Danvers who's so passionate
about everything she does--

00:01:58.740 --> 00:01:59.980 line:84%
NANCY WILSON: Exactly.
- --about flying.

00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:04.170 line:84%
 With a guitar, I feel like
a superhero who could fly.

00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:05.560 line:90%
 Yeah.

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:07.880 line:84%
 I really relate to the
character in the movie a lot.

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:08.680 line:90%
Yeah.

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:10.520 line:84%
 Well, thank you so much
for talking with us, Nancy.

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:11.320 line:90%
 Thanks.

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:12.587 line:84%
TAMARA KRINSKY: This
has been a blast.

